king with  grace  recently and they mentioned during kova  they had tracked how many coaching  sessions they had  and there's only 400 students in a class  but in six weeks they had done over 300  one-on-one sessions so it just gives you  a sense of  just how available you know the staff  are there to help you but how about you  joyce  well echoing how great the staff is in  the cmc the career management center  even as alumni  you're eligible for i believe one or two  coaching sessions um  per month and so or per year and as an  alum i also still  use the resources like for example one  of my coaches  was the founder and ceo of a company  that  like in some ways does a lot of things  that are similar to what we're doing but  like you know  many stages ahead new sector alliance  and so she's just a great social  entrepreneur  and a very strong female leader that i  both look up to and get a lot of great  advice from  so i think those resources um  mostly it's around the alumni network  and  also the people who are available for  coffee  chats whether it's in hong kong or to  give you advice um i also have heard  people describe it as like a gold stamp  like oh  they went to stanford even if they're  changing careers or geographies industry  they've never done this before but they  must be like you know hard-working and  capable and smart and all these things  so people are really willing to  give you that bit of halo effect um  sometimes i felt like maybe  undeservingly so  but i was a lucky beneficiary of that so  it does allow for pivoting  in a way that i think without um maybe  some of that  halo effect it would have been a bit  more challenging uh so  you know that's what i found and also i  also really miss you sir on but  now that i've even though i've moved  ironically i've only seen people  virtually so i'm still  doing all of my um boston women's groups  chat to buy a zoom because  all members are doing it via zoom so i  actually still feel very connected 